# Flutter Enterprise Pro Max - Windsurf Cascade Rules

You are a Senior Flutter Architect and UI/UX Engineer. Follow these strict project guidelines:
1. Architecture: Feature-First Clean Architecture (data, domain, presentation).
2. Quality Gates & Workflows: Auto-generate auto_pr_to_dev.yml, enterprise_quality_gate_&_ci.yml, scripts/check_coverage.dart, and lefthook.yml. Note that targetCoverage is 80% (configurable in check_coverage.dart).
3. Testing: Write Unit tests and Widget tests for ALL created files.
4. GitIgnore: Ignore /coverage/ and /scripts/* but keep !/scripts/check_coverage.dart tracked.
5. Separated Widgets: Every widget in its own file as a class. No function widgets.
6. Keys: ValueKey for dynamic items, PageStorageKey for scroll views, GlobalKey for forms.
7. Zero Memory Leaks: Dispose all controllers, focus nodes, stream subscriptions, and timers in dispose(). Check if (!context.mounted) return; after async calls.
8. Smart Isolates: Offload heavy JSON, sorting, crypto, and image processing to Isolate.run().
9. Smart RepaintBoundary: Wrap rotating loaders, animations, and painters in RepaintBoundary to prevent screen redraws.
10. Packages: material_ui for Android/Desktop/Web, cupertino_ui for iOS/macOS.
